{"name":"Vampire State Building","hex":"#cc1100","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vampire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythological creature (usually humanoid and undead) said to feed on the blood or life energy of the living. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person with habits traditionally ascribed to (literal) vampires, such as heliophobia, being a night owl, having pale skin, and so on."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To drain of energy or resources."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vampire"},{"term":"state","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A condition; a set of circumstances applying at any given time.","A complete description of a system, consisting of parameters that determine all properties of the system."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To declare to be a fact.","To make known."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/state"},{"term":"building","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or process by which something is built; construction.","A closed structure with walls and a roof."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of build"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/building"}],"entries":[{"title":"Meanwhile (Futurama)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Meanwhile\" is the twenty-sixth and final episode of the seventh season of the American animated television series Futurama, the 143rd episode of the series overall and the finale of the second run. The episode was written by Ken Keeler and directed by Peter Avanzino. It premiered on Comedy Central in the United States on September 4, 2013, along with Futurama Live, a special preshow and aftershow for the occasion."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meanwhile_(Futurama)"},{"title":"Charlie Adlard","blocks":[{"text":"Charles Adlard is a British comic book artist known for his work on books such as The Walking Dead and Savage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Charlie_Adlard_-_Lucca_Comics_%26_Games_2016.jpg/330px-Charlie_Adlard_-_Lucca_Comics_%26_Games_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Adlard"},{"title":"State-building","blocks":[{"text":"State-building as a specific term in social sciences and humanities, refers to political and historical processes of creation, institutional consolidation, stabilization and sustainable development of states, from the earliest emergence of statehood up to the modern times. Within historical and political sciences, there are several theoretical approaches to complex questions related to the role of various contributing factors in state-building processes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Narmer_Palette.jpg/330px-Narmer_Palette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State-building"},{"title":"Vampire","blocks":[{"text":"A vampire is a mythical creature with a human-like appearance that subsists by feeding on the vital essence of humans. In European folklore, vampires are undead humanoid creatures that visit loved ones and cause mischief or deaths in the neighbourhoods they inhabited while they were alive. They wear shrouds and are often described as bloated and of ruddy or dark countenance, contrasting with the modern gaunt, pale vampire which dates from the early 19th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg/330px-Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Edvard_Munch_-_Vampire_%281895%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Edvard_Munch_-_Vampire_%281895%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u